---
description: Run Cursor review bots on the whole repository
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository uses Cursor's review bots on the **entire tree**, not a subdirectory.

When the user asks to review, or before opening a pull request:

1. Run `/review-bugbot` (Bugbot) against branch changes vs the default base branch.
2. Run `/review-security` (Security Review) against the same diff.
3. Use `/review` only when you need the appropriate reviewer chosen automatically.

Project files those bots read:

- `.cursor/BUGBOT.md` — Bugbot rules for every path
- `APPROVAL_POLICY.md` and `.cursor/approval-policies/ROUTING.md` — PR Routing & Approval

Do not treat a local `/review-*` run as enabling the GitHub bots. Enable Bugbot, Security Agents, and PR Routing for this repository in Cursor, and turn on auto-enable for new repositories.
